WEBVTT

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:02.730
We’ll win.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.020
Who are you?

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.860
Who are you?

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.070
Astral.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.420
Astral?

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.870
If my memory is correct.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.790
What are you talking about?

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.280
What’s wrong, Yuma?

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.580
Why are you talking to yourself?

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.790
You can’t see him?

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.300
Right here!

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.260
Someone’s there?

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.550
Yeah!

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.820
He’s dressed weird!

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:38.850
Right here!

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.490
Maybe he lost his mind because he’s scared.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.720
I’m not scared!

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.940
Only I can see him?

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.730
Did my D-Gazer break?

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.800
It seems you’re unable to
comprehend my existence.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.030
Can it be that you’re...

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.410
My name is Yuma Tsukumo!

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.470
I’m a first-year middle schooler who’s gonna
kattobing to become a dueling champion!

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.580
I have to duel because I wagered
the deck my father left me.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.920
But my opponent is Shark,
a guy who made the nationals!

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.010
I was in a bad situation
when someone suddenly appeared!

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.720
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard
or the scorching sun

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.850
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.770
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.020
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:39.410
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.040
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:52.500
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.380
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.510
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.480
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.600
Everyone is not the same

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.600
That’s the reason for living

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.860
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:20.280
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.290
I travel to the edge of the world

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:28.000
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.040
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard
or the scorching sun

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.380
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.380
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.590
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.560
Can it be?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.160
You’re a ghost!

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.100
Ghost?

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.910
My Name is Astral

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.910
Number 2:

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:54.910
My Name is Astral

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.610
What kind of effect is “ghost?”

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.370
When does it activate?

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.980
What are you talking about?

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.860
It seems I’ve lost my memories.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.070
It happened when I came to this world.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.200
A collision must’ve sent my memories flying.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.230
Lost your memories?

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.850
And memories can fly?

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.740
This is bad!

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.490
There’s something wrong with me!

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.270
Why did this have to happen
during an important duel?

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.180
Calm down.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.550
It’s your fault!

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.290
Is Yuma okay?

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.520
He’s still talking to himself.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.600
Fighting Shark was too much
for him to handle.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.620
Tetsuo, you can’t lose heart either!

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.900
Yuma and your decks are
on the line in this duel!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.860
We can’t let Shark take them!

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.740
Pull yourself together, Yuma!

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.850
I am pulled together!

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.750
It seems I’m the only one who can see him.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:58.380
And Shark changed when that
Number Card appeared.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.090
Number 17: Leviathan Dragon.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.050
After this Xyz Monster appeared,
I’m overflowing with power!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:12.140
I don’t think I’ll lose against anyone!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.810
I’ll take your deck!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.980
I set one card and end my turn.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.200
Numbers...

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.240
I think I remembered something
important about them.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.580
My instincts tell me that
I must win this duel.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.540
You know about dueling?

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.250
Yes. I’m a duelist.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:40.960
A ghost duelist?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.630
I’m a duelist!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.640
My turn!

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.470
It’s my turn!

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.260
My turn! I draw!

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.650
I set Gogogo Golem in defense position!

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.770
Don’t butt in on my duel!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.920
I summon Gogogo Golem in attack position!

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.200
It can’t defeat his monster because
it only has 1800 ATK.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.040
I know that!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.160
I activate the spell card
Blustering Winds from my hand!

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:23.090
With Blustering Winds, one monster in attack position gains 1000 ATK until my next turn!

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.050
Yuma, this is your chance!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.840
Go, Gogogo Golem!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.050
Attack Leviathan Dragon!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.850
All right! Leviathan Dragon is destroyed!

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.860
This is the first time
I lowered Shark’s life points!

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.760
Hooray!

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.190
Look.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.900
What?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.830
Even though he took away his life points,
why isn’t his monster destroyed?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:55.200
If they’re both in attack position,
the monster with higher ATK wins!

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.490
Wait a second!

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.130
Leviathan Dragon is supposed to be destroyed!

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:02.020
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.090
A Number can only be destroyed
by another Number.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:09.340
What? I don’t have a Number!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.540
Only a Number can defeat a Number?

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.350
What is he going to do?

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:17.510
Numbers don’t matter!

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:21.310
Gogogo Golem has more
ATK than Leviathan Dragon!

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.230
Gogogo Golem will be destroyed
on the next turn.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:34.040
If he has a monster in his hand with 800 or more ATK, there’s no way we can win this duel.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.950
I have 1000 LP!

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:43.130
Observation #1: Your dueling tactics
are far inferior to mine.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.380
Inferior?

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.590
What does tactics mean?

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.300
It means strategy.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.040
Oh, strategy.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.110
Strategy...

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:54.760
What did you say?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.020
I’ll end the duel with this!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.270
My turn! I draw!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.370
I summon Drill Barnacle!

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.900
300 ATK.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.030
You’re lucky.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.860
What are you talking about?

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.490
Leviathan Dragon’s effect activates!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.490
I use an Overlay Unit!

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.450
It gains 500 ATK!

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.110
3000 ATK? Are you serious?

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:25.840
Leviathan Dragon had one Overlay Unit left.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:30.410
It was obvious that he would use that
effect to increase its ATK.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.800
Really?

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.300
Go, Leviathan Dragon!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.560
Attack Gogogo Golem!

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.300
I’m down to 800 LP.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.490
He knew this was going to happen.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.200
I still have an attack remaining!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.080
Drill Barnacle!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.660
Drill Attack!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.010
Damn...

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.710
Yuma...

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:10.920
When Gogogo Golem is in defense position,
its effect prevents it from being destroyed by battle once.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:17.190
If you brought out Gogogo Golem in defense position as I instructed, you wouldn’t be in this difficult situation.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.390
Shut up!

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.060
What’s this?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.630
I’m losing my life.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:29.700
Numbers...

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.290
I remember.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:40.030
Numbers are pieces of my memories.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:45.350
Numbers are special cards,
even among Xyz Monsters.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:48.540
The cards in this world cannot defeat them.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:54.800
In a duel between Numbers,
the winner absorbs the loser’s Number.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.470
What do you mean?

00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:02.480
If you don’t win this duel,
I will vanish from this world.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.640
I must win this duel.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.110
I’ve been trying to win from the start!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.880
But I don’t have a card in my hand
for a counterattack.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.700
If I can stop Leviathan Dragon’s
attack next turn...

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.580
...even if Drill Barnacle attacks me,
I’ll still have 200 LP left.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.790
There’s no point in thinking!

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:25.890
I activate Drill Barnacle’s effect!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:31.210
When it deals you damage,
it gains 1000 ATK.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:36.570
Furthermore, Drill Barnacle
can attack you directly.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:40.510
If the direct attack succeeds next turn,
you’re finished.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.720
Are you serious?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.230
If I take that attack, I’ll lose!

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.910
What should I do?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.520
I have a trap card set!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.550
What was this card again?

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.690
Bye Bye Damage.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:10:01.910
If you had activated it, not only would you have dealt him damage, but Gogogo Golem wouldn’t have been destroyed.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:05.120
I forgot because you keep talking to me!

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:08.120
Just give up on this duel already!

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.910
I’m never giving up!

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:12.100
You still think you can win?

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:14.300
I’ll never give up!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.040
Never give up...

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.800
Those words annoy me.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.230
Anyway...

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:22.260
There’s still a chance.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:26.080
You must summon two monsters.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.980
Listen closely... Umm...

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.810
My name is Yuma!

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:31.810
Listen closely...

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:32.980
Idiot.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.780
My name isn’t idiot! It’s Yuma!

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.990
On your next draw, get a card that allows
you to Special Summon a monster.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.000
A card that lets me Special Summon?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.400
You must draw a card that can do that.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.000
Be quiet!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:50.450
My deck and Tetsuo’s
are on the line in this duel!

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.670
My turn! I draw!

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:54.840
Monster Reborn.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.840
Destiny hasn’t forsaken me.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.800
I’m the one who drew it!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.700
I summon Ganbara Knight in attack position!

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.560
Why in attack position, Yuma?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.230
Ganbara Knight has 0 ATK!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.940
Oh no!

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.310
It looks like I win.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.440
Give up!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.470
I’ll never give up!

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.400
I can always kattobing!

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:22.130
Kattobing?

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.450
Kattobing means to keep challenging!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.150
My heart never gives up!

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:30.410
If you give up, your heart dies!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.410
You’re so annoying.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:37.710
People who don’t give up annoy me the most!

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:43.690
How are you going to fight against
my monsters when your monster has 0 ATK?

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:46.060
It’s fine.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:51.890
If you summoned it in defense position,
we would’ve lost our chance at a comeback...

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.150
Idiot.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.610
It’s Yuma!

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:57.840
Use Monster Reborn to resurrect Gagaga Magician.

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.820
What?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.960
I can’t allow myself to disappear.

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.780
Trust me.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:09.500
I’m not doing this because I trust you.

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:13.460
I activate the spell card
Monster Reborn from my hand!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.580
I resurrect Gagaga Magician from my graveyard!

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:22.260
What’s the point of bringing out
a monster with 1500 ATK?

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.260
The requirements have been met.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:25.260
What?

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:29.430
Overlay Level 4 Gagaga Magician
and Ganbara Knight.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.440
Are you talking about an Xyz Summon?

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:34.100
Look at your Extra Deck.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:39.570
What’s this Xyz Monster?

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.580
I can’t read the text.

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:43.590
I can read it.

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:47.150
Number 39: Utopia.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:50.240
This is a Number?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.710
That’s right. You were given that power.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.750
I’m counting on you!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.910
I’m kattobing!

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:03.960
I overlay Level 4 Gagaga Magician
and Ganbara Knight!

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.920
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.180
Xyz Summon!

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:15.140
Appear, Number 39: Utopia!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.290
Go, Utopia!

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.170
Attack Drill Barnacle!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.510
Hope Sword Slash!

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:58.350
Hooray!

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:00.110
Shark took a lot of damage!

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.020
A Number?

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:08.990
Utopia is the key to defeating
Leviathan Dragon!

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.440
Another Number?

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.200
Utopia?

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.680
Did Yuma have that card?

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.920
I don’t think he did.

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.670
I end my turn!

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:27.590
That was the first Xyz Summon in my life!

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.360
Hey, did you see it?

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.560
I saw it!

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:32.560
I know you did!

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.730
It was worth it to kattobing!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.060
What are you so happy about?

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.800
Utopia has 2500 ATK.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:44.900
Leviathan Dragon has 3000 ATK,
so it’s all over if it attacks.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.400
Oh yeah! That’s bad!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:51.030
Even though you summoned a Number,
you’re not good enough to defeat me!

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.660
My turn! I draw!

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.410
I activate the spell card Surface from my hand!

00:14:57.410 --> 00:15:02.340
This card Special Summons a WATER monster
from my graveyard in defense position!

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.300
Resurrect, Big Jaws!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.930
Next, I tribute Big Jaws.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.640
I Tribute Summon Jawsman!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:18.890
Tribute Summon?

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:24.950
It’s a summoning method where you tribute
a monster to summon a higher Level monster.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:34.120
It gains 300 ATK for every
WATER monster on my field other than itself.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.490
Leviathan Dragon’s attribute is WATER.

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.290
Therefore, Jawsman has 2900 ATK!

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.230
I’ll finish you!

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:45.340
First, Leviathan Dragon attacks Utopia!

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.510
Doesn’t Utopia have some kind of effect?

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:58.600
Utopia’s effect negates a monster’s
attack by using an Overlay Unit.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.560
Say that earlier!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.650
I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:08.410
I use an Overlay Unit to negate
Leviathan Dragon’s attack!

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.120
Moon Barrier!

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.710
So that’s Utopia’s effect.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:27.840
But even if you avoid my attacks,
you can’t win if you don’t defeat my monster!

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.550
Defeat his monster...

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:34.260
You only have one Overlay Unit left to use.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:39.850
A non-Number can’t destroy a Number,
but it can still deal damage.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:44.060
If you want to avoid taking damage,
use your remaining Overlay Unit!

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:47.270
Go, Jawsman! Attack Utopia!

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:51.230
Do what he says and use Utopia’s effect again!

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:54.160
How to defeat his monster...

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.060
All right!

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:59.910
I activate the trap card Bye Bye Damage!

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:06.240
With Bye Bye Damage, one monster on my field
won’t be destroyed by battle this turn!

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:09.340
Why didn’t you use Utopia’s effect?

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.800
I can do whatever I want!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:21.510
If I take battle damage,
you take double the damage!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.650
Yuma only has 100 LP left.

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:34.700
Since you activated a trap, I can activate
the Continuous Trap Explosive Urchin!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:40.210
When it becomes my turn,
this trap deals you 1000 points of damage.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.700
Now my victory is assured!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.920
It’s no good. Yuma is going to lose.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.490
Oh no!

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:48.960
Yuma...

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.750
Give up.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.260
I’m not giving up yet!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.650
You only have one turn left.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:58.640
Why won’t you give up on this duel?

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:00.340
What about you?

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:03.390
Why do you want me to give up?

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:08.060
It must mean that you’ve given up on something!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.940
You must have given up on something important!

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:21.130
Since I never give up, I can always kattobing!

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:23.080
I’ll show you!

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.430
There’s a way to make a comeback?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:26.710
There is!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.630
A combo in my deck that will defeat him!

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:32.670
Grandma...

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.260
Take it.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.590
Yuma, what are you doing?

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:43.550
This is my fighting food!

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.270
It’s duel food!

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.920
I’m completely charged!

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:51.420
My turn!

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:56.860
Now’s my only chance to defeat him!

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.360
I’m kattobing!

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.490
I draw!

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.870
Here it is!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:07.960
Go!

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:11.790
Utopia, attack Leviathan Dragon!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.250
Unbelievable!

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:16.370
Why?

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.780
Utopia has less ATK!

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:21.800
Next, I activate Utopia’s effect!

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:26.680
I use an Overlay Unit to negate
Utopia’s attack!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.690
What’s the point of a combo
that doesn’t deal damage?

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.660
There’s a huge point!

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:37.350
From my hand, I activate
the Quick-Play Spell, Double or Nothing!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.700
A Quick-Play Spell?

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:48.200
When a monster’s attack is negated,
its ATK is doubled, and it can attack again!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.580
5000 ATK?

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.500
Utopia, kattobing!

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:59.260
Attack Leviathan Dragon!

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:15.820
Did I win?

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.810
Yuma...

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:18.960
Won?

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.520
I won!

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:24.560
I beat Shark!

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:27.080
Kattobing!

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:30.450
You lost to <i>him?</i>

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.250
You’ve fallen far, Shark!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.140
This is the Number 17 card.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.380
It’s a piece of my memories.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:21:02.510
If I gather the 99 Number cards,
my memories will return.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.300
Amazing!

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:09.760
I lost...

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.310
Mom and Dad, I won.

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:18.040
Shark...

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.000
As I promised.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:24.760
I’ll take Tetsuo’s deck back.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:28.470
Yuma Tsukumo, I’ll remember you.

00:21:29.110 --> 00:21:32.680
Shark, that was really fun!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.680
Let’s duel again sometime.

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:37.730
But let’s not wager our decks next time.

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.690
Let’s kattobing together!

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:49.120
You’re willing to risk everything
by trusting in a single draw.

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:53.090
You seem different.

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:54.930
Well, whatever.

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:56.500
I was great!

00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:01.840
You’re a duelist that exceeded my expectations...

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.300
Idiot.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.860
My name isn’t idiot!

00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:10.010
It’s Yuma!

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:15.170
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.920 --> 00:22:17.530
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:20.740
These numbers are important for monsters.

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:23.020
ATK stands for attack points.

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.360
What does this stand for?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:34.800
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:39.920
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:54.420
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.420 --> 00:22:59.520
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:01.940
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.570
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.250
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.250 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.600
Let’s say I wrote the
correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:18.080
Will that change the future
a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.550
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.130
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:37.130
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:46.480
This ghost duelist is with me when I’m awake,
sleeping and even when I’m eating!

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:48.680
Yuma, gather the Numbers.

00:23:48.680 --> 00:23:49.990
Be quiet!

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:53.780
That’s when a computer virus
was unleashed into the city!

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:56.440
Who’s doing this? And why?

00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:57.820
Just wait!

00:23:57.820 --> 00:24:00.450
I’m going to capture the criminal!

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:10.010
To Summarize, It’s a Case!!

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:05.710
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“To Summarize, It’s a Case!!”

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hTo Summarize, It’s a Case!!\h\h

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:10.010
To Summarize, It’s a Case!!

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:08.130
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:15.490
DEF stands for defense points!

00:24:15.490 --> 00:24:20.440
The higher the number, the stronger its defense.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:22.440
Dueling isn’t just about attacking!

00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:24.720
Defense is also important!
